  "lowtech.weight": "Low-tech mode · <strong>{size}</strong> transferred since opening · system font, vector drawings, no trackers. <a href=\"#/lowtech\">Why?</a>",
  "lowtech.title": "Why a low-tech Web?",
  "lowtech.html": "<h1>Why a low-tech Web?</h1><p>Every page you open sets servers, networks and, above all, the device in your hand to work. A lighter Web asks less energy of each of these links, and lets less powerful phones stay in use for longer.</p><h2>The weight of digital technology</h2><ul><li>In France, according to the 2022 ADEME–Arcep study, the <strong>manufacture and use of devices</strong> (phones, computers, screens) account for the largest share of the carbon footprint of digital technology, far ahead of networks and data centres.</li><li>Heavier pages push people to replace their devices: a site that stays smooth on an old phone extends its lifespan.</li><li>A median web page now weighs around <strong>2 MB</strong> on mobile, mostly images and scripts: much of it is not needed for what you came to read.</li></ul><h2>The Low-tech Magazine example</h2><p>The <a href=\"https://solar.lowtechmagazine.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Low-tech Magazine<span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (new tab)</span></a> website is hosted on a small server powered by a solar panel. To run on that energy, it was redesigned:</p><ul><li><strong>static site</strong>: pages are prepared in advance, nothing is computed on each visit;</li><li><strong>dithered images</strong> in a few shades of grey, much lighter than colour photos;</li><li>the system's <strong>default font</strong>, no font to download, and no image logo;</li><li><strong>no trackers</strong>, no advertising, no third-party services;</li><li>it accepts being <strong>offline</strong> when the sky stays cloudy for too long, and shows its battery level.</li></ul><p>To find out more: <a href=\"https://solar.lowtechmagazine.com/2018/09/how-to-build-a-low-tech-website/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How to Build a Low-tech Website?<span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (new tab)</span></a></p><p class=\"hint\">As the site runs on sunshine, it may be offline after several days without sun: that is intentional. Try again later.</p><h2>What this mode does</h2><ul><li>System font and two inks: no colours, shadows, gradients or animations.</li><li>Card backs rendered as text, with a simplified line drawing of less than 1 kB built into the page, instead of a 30 kB colour image.</li><li>Decorative images (home page fan, thumbnails) are not downloaded.</li><li>In dark theme, a pure black background: on OLED screens, black pixels are switched off.</li><li>The timer redraws once per second instead of four times.</li><li>Everywhere, the app only loads the QR code library on screens that show one, and keeps its files in cache to work offline.</li></ul><h2>The figures for this app</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"weights\"><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Journey</th><th scope=\"col\">Before</th><th scope=\"col\">Normal</th><th scope=\"col\">Low-tech</th></tr></thead><tbody> {rows} </tbody></table></div><p class=\"hint\">“Before”: the version of the app preceding this mode. Data transferred on a first visit, files compressed as on GitHub Pages. Since this page was opened, your phone has transferred <strong>{size}</strong> (0 kB for what comes from the cache).</p><h2>And you, what would an efficient Web look like?</h2><p>A few questions to look ahead, linked to the <em>Environmental impact</em> golden rule:</p><ul class=\"questions\"><li>Which tools do you use every day that could work with fewer images, videos or scripts?</li><li>For your uses of AI, when would a lighter model, or no AI at all, be enough?</li><li>Would you accept a service that is sometimes unavailable, like Low-tech Magazine, if it used much less energy?</li><li>What would the “low-tech” version of a project you are working on look like?</li></ul>",
